cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: Water Tenure Storymap
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
abstract: >-
  Water Tenure Storymap is open-source software for publishing a water tenure
  assessment as an interactive map and a set of map-driven stories. It
  consists of a tenure engine (a FastAPI service that stores tenure records
  classified on the FAO water tenure typology and geotagged field photos,
  validates them against a controlled vocabulary, and generalizes the location
  of sensitive records) and a configurable Next.js storymap whose site
  settings, map layers, stories and gallery are content files. It ships with a
  synthetic example basin and an importer for water tenure catalogues. The
  software was vibe-coded: the code and documentation were written by AI coding
  agents (Claude Code with Anthropic Claude models, operated as CRPG's agent
  "Mobot") under the orchestration of Mohamad Mova Al'Afghani, who set the
  goals, the method and the domain rules and directed and reviewed the work.
type: software
